# Customer Segmentation Using Clustering Algorithms

An unsupervised machine learning project that analyzes mall customer 
purchasing behavior and identifies meaningful customer segments using 
clustering techniques to support targeted marketing strategies.

---

## Research Objective
Analyze customer purchasing behavior and identify distinct customer 
groups using clustering algorithms, then develop tailored marketing 
strategies for each segment.

---

## Dataset
**Mall Customer Segmentation Dataset**
- 200 customer records
- 5 features: CustomerID, Gender, Age, Annual Income (k$), Spending Score (1-100)
- Source: [Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/vjchoudhary7/customer-segmentation-tutorial-in-python)

---

## Project Structure

customer-segmentation-clustering/

│

├── Customer_Segmentation.ipynb   # Main Jupyter Notebook

├── Mall_Customers.csv            # Dataset

├── app.py                        # Streamlit application (in progress)

├── requirements.txt              # Python dependencies

├── README.md                     # Project documentation

│

└── models/

├── kmeans_model.pkl          # Saved K-Means model

├── scaler.pkl                # Fitted StandardScaler

├── dbscan_model.pkl          # Saved DBSCAN model

├── hierarchical_model.pkl    # Saved Hierarchical model

└── segmented_customers.csv  # Final segmented dataset

---

## Methodology

### 1. Exploratory Data Analysis
- Distribution analysis of Age, Income, and Spending Score
- Gender distribution and spending comparison
- Correlation heatmap
- Outlier detection using IQR method
- Spending patterns by age group

### 2. Preprocessing
- Dropped CustomerID (non-informative)
- Label encoded Gender (Female=0, Male=1)
- Applied StandardScaler to all numeric features
- Defined two feature sets:
  - **X_2d** — Income + Spending Score (for K-Means)
  - **X_full** — All 4 features (for DBSCAN)

### 3. Finding Optimal Clusters
- Elbow Method — clear bend at k=5
- Silhouette Score — peak of 0.55 at k=5
- Both methods confirmed k=5

### 4. Clustering Algorithms

| Algorithm | Feature Set | Parameters | Silhouette |
|---|---|---|---|
| K-Means | X_2d | k=5, k-means++ | 0.5547 |
| DBSCAN | X_full | eps=0.8, min_samples=5 | 0.4821 |
| Hierarchical | X_full | Ward linkage, n=5 | 0.5102 |

---

## Results — Customer Segments

| Cluster | Segment | Age | Income | Spending | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Average Customer | 43 | 55k | 50 | Medium |
| 1 | High Income, High Spender | 33 | 87k | 82 | Highest |
| 2 | Young, Low Income, High Spender | 25 | 26k | 79 | High |
| 3 | High Income, Low Spender | 41 | 88k | 17 | High Potential |
| 4 | Middle-Aged, Low Income, Low Spender | 45 | 26k | 21 | Low |

> DBSCAN additionally identified **13 outlier customers** who do not 
> fit any segment and require individual attention.

---

## Marketing Strategies

| Segment | Strategy |
|---|---|
| High Income, High Spender | VIP loyalty program, exclusive perks, premium campaigns |
| Young, Low Income, High Spender | Social media, influencer campaigns, buy-now-pay-later |
| High Income, Low Spender | Premium quality messaging, exclusive bundles, incentives |
| Average Customer | Seasonal promotions, upselling, loyalty points |
| Middle-Aged, Low Income, Low Spender | Budget deals, SMS promotions, clearance sales |

---

## Streamlit App
An interactive web app where you can input customer details and 
instantly receive their predicted segment and marketing recommendation.

> ⚠️ Currently functional but under active improvement. 
> UI enhancements and additional features are in progress.

### Run locally:
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```

